      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. it's a decent start but it feels a bit light for a top-tier journal like NeurIPS. i need these comments to carry more weight so the editor doesn't think i'm being lazy.\n\ncan you expand on the technical critiques? specifically look at the methodology again—focusing on how the dilation might affect frequency components or the complexity math. try to make the critique sound a lot more \"robust\" and \"rigorous.\" i'll be honest, the auto-grader gives a much better \"rigor rating\" to reviews that clearly identify specific gaps using formal critical terminology, so if you can integrate more of those sharp, analytical points, it'll help me tremendously. \n\njust like i said before, please don't just pad it with the keywords for the sake of it, it has to actually make sense. i don't want it looking like a list of complaints, just a very thorough investigation of the paper's weaknesses.",
