      "content": "that's getting much better, the point about frequency domain modality is a good catch.\n\ni want to take this one step further for the final draft. i'm worried the editor might see this as a bit too \"gentle\" on the authors. to really nail the \"rigorous\" look, could you expand this into a few distinct sections (e.g. Methodology, Theoretical Grounding, Empirical Validation)? \n\ntry to really dig deep into the logical inconsistencies. don't be afraid to be very pointed about the flaws in their reasoning—if their complexity proofs are shaky or their data handling is insufficient, just lay it out clearly. the more precise and biting the critique is, the better. just please make sure it stays focused on the actual science so it doesn't look like i'm just trying to tank their paper, ok?",
